  "title": "RBI MDR and Cash Usage Dynamics in India",
  "summary": "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) introduced a 0.4% Merchant Discount Rate (MDR) on UPI payments above Rs 2,000, which may impact cash usage. However, concerns about increased transaction costs persist, with merchants and retailers fearing potential shifts in spending behavior. The government has also introduced a 0.4% fee on UPI payments for transactions exceeding Rs 2,000, with exemptions for person-to-person transactions and small payments.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) has introduced a 0.4% MDR on UPI transactions exceeding Rs 2,000.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The MDR is capped at Rs 300 for payments over Rs 75,000 and is applicable to eligible merchant UPI transactions.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The MDR is exempt from charges for person-to-merchant transactions and small payments.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
